    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-10-31T09:20:31+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-31T09:20:31+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-30T22:50:31Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-30T22:50:31Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A low pressure system south of the Bight extends a trough over far southeast of state and will continue to move east clearing the state this morning, followed by a new high pressure system. Another low pressure system is expected to enter from the west on Sunday, moving over central and eastern districts on Monday, followed by another ridge of high pressure which will persist until Tuesday.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW010" description="West Coast" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-10-31T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-01T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-30T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-31T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Sunny. Winds northwest to northeasterly 15 to 25 km/h tending southeast to southwesterly 15 to 20 km/h in the late afternoon then tending northeast to southeasterly in the evening. Daytime maximum temperatures 27 to 35.</text>
                <text type="fire_danger">Moderate</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:20am to 5:10pm, UV Index predicted to reach 11 [Extreme]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-11-01T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-02T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-31T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-01T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. Medium chance of showers south of Streaky Bay, most likely in the morning and afternoon. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm from the late morning. Winds east to northeasterly 25 to 40 km/h tending northwest to northeasterly in the middle of the day then tending northwest to southwesterly in the early afternoon. Overnight temperatures falling to between 14 and 20 with daytime temperatures reaching 32 to 38.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-11-02T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-03T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-01T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-02T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. Winds west to southwesterly 15 to 20 km/h tending south to southwesterly 25 to 35 km/h during the day. Overnight temperatures falling to around 14 with daytime temperatures reaching 25 to 30.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-11-03T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-04T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-02T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-03T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. The chance of morning fog east of Ceduna. Winds southeast to southwesterly 15 to 20 km/h tending northwest to southwesterly 15 to 25 km/h during the morning then tending southeast to southwesterly during the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 10 and 13 with daytime temperatures reaching 26 to 33.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
